Z||000000||MooCow||01-15-2001||03:07 PM||||All the way home from Ed Parks the car ran awsome.  I pulled it into my driveway and my dad jumps in it.  He started pushing the lights on.  Tho ones by the sunroof.  Then he turned them off and started the car up and the door light came on.  The light by the gas pedals.  After he shut the door the gas pedal lights were still on and now the sunroof light won't turn on at all.  Also I couldn't get the gas pedal lights to turn off so I had to pull the bulb out.  How happened?  Also now the power locks don't work.  Could it be a blown fuse?  I need to fix this quick before my parnets find out cause they were mad that I spend $4,600 on my new GT.<P>                              Thanks Ken||||reg||9
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-15-2001||03:23 PM||||Call Ed Parks.. Sounds like a ground problem in the wiring for the light circuit.  Unless you want to interpret the wiring diagram from the Haynes manual and fix it yourself.||||reg||3
Z||000002||stsmithgt||01-15-2001||03:59 PM||||Check your fuses.  those lights go on and the door locks and trunk release won't work when this certain fuse is blown.  It's around the front left side of the fuse box.  I need to double check the fuse size in mine, but I have a yellow (10 amp.) fuse in that position.  Strange doings huh?||||reg||14
Z||000003||pHoOl||01-15-2001||04:54 PM||||Are you going to come to the little GR gathering on friday?  I knwo that we'd like to see it.  <P>------------------<BR>AIM: phool88fiero<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||01-15-2001||05:20 PM||||If the Ctsy fuse blows you'll lose the trunk release (and door locks I believe) and the reading lights will act up like yours.  This is because two circuits share the same ground.  If the fuse blows on one circuit the ground completes through the bulbs in the reading light and makes the interior lights act strange.<P>Replace the fuse and all should be back to normal.  Also find out why the fuse blew to start with.<P>I recently bought an 85GT where most power accessories would not work.  Replacing the ctsy fuse fixed just about everything.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
